AFTER-ACTION REPORT — PAIN'S ASSAULT ON KONOHAGAKURE
Classification: Archive — Restricted

Event: The Akatsuki leader known as "Pain" (the Six Paths of Pain,
directed by Nagato of the Hidden Rain) launched a direct assault on the
village in search of the Nine-Tails jinchuriki, Naruto Uzumaki.

Course of Events:
- The Six Paths infiltrated and, using the Almighty Push (Shinra Tensei),
  leveled much of the village, inflicting mass destruction and casualties.
- The Godaime Hokage, Tsunade, defended the villagers to the point of
  chakra exhaustion, protecting the population with Katsuyu.
- Naruto Uzumaki returned from Sage training at Mount Myoboku, defeated
  the Six Paths, and confronted Nagato directly.
- Moved by Naruto's conviction, Nagato used the Samsara of Heavenly Life
  technique to restore those who had died in the attack, at the cost of
  his own life.

Aftermath: The village was rebuilt. Naruto was hailed as a hero. Losses
were grievous but reversed. Retained as the definitive record of the
event. See Intelligence's Akatsuki activity log.
